blocks.body:
Under inversion with centre $O$ and radius $r$:

1. a line through $O$ is mapped to itself;
2. a line not through $O$ is mapped to a circle through $O$, and a circle through $O$ to a line not through $O$;
3. a circle not through $O$ is mapped to a circle not through $O$.

In each case the point $O$ itself is left out. Moreover, for points $P, Q \ne O$,
$$P'Q' = \frac{r^2\,PQ}{OP\cdot OQ}.$$
